;; Every function of tools/kexe_loader.c, classified (superproject
;; adr-2609251400 C1). scripts/test-loader-decisions.cljk fails on a function
;; that is not named here and on a name here that no longer exists, and
;; prints the per-class line counts before (the loader at 0d244a95, whose
;; decisions were C) and after.
;;
;;   :mechanism  decides nothing: mmap / fork / signals / syscalls / sandbox
;;               installation, handle and arena bookkeeping, memory-safety
;;               bounds (a handle resolves, an index is inside its slice, a
;;               copy fits its buffer), pure computation with a published
;;               definition (SHA-256, Ed25519, UTF-8 scanning), and CALLING a
;;               decision.
;;   :decision   the function IS a rule someone chose: a limit, a vocabulary,
;;               a policy, a name.
;;   :mixed      mechanism with a rule inside it.
;;
;; :before is the class at 0d244a95 when it differs; :moved names what went
;; to Kotoba (tools/kexe_loader_decisions.kotoba / _names.kotoba) and how:
;; (a) data evaluated into the generated region, (b) code the loader calls.
;; :left names a rule still in C. :new marks the glue this change added.
;; The classification is judgement, recorded so it can be argued with.
